Gabriel Cabezas (cello)", "title": "November 1 (Homesick)", "artist": "Elliot Cole", "artwork": {"nft": null, "info": {"uri": "https://ipfs.io/ipfs/bafybeifusydp5qsa5t2ifup35q3vixqtzieyqtzucvz3jsosa57cl7dgmu", "mimeType": "image/png"}, "isNft": false}, "project": {"notes": "I keep a staff paper notebook and use it like a personal diary. When I have a quiet moment I sketch tunes about people, travels, and life experiences. It's almost never for public ears - it's a place where I get to think about music without trying to impress other people. This album opens a small window into that private world.", "title": "Journals (vol. 1)", "artwork": {"nft": null, "info": {"uri": "https://ipfs.io/ipfs/bafybeifusydp5qsa5t2ifup35q3vixqtzieyqtzucvz3jsosa57cl7dgmu", "mimeType": "image/png"}, "isNft": false}}, "version": "catalog-20210202", "duration": 150.073, "mimeType": "audio/wav", "visualizer": null, "trackNumber": 1}, "origin": {"encoding": "rlp", "algorithm": "secp256k1", "publicKey": "0xc236541380fc0C2C05c2F2c6c52a21ED57c37952", "signature": "0xb240b3f49db98d27218e65214c1d5bea4bb5520b0c7a909fe5d86d093d90b85717af48b0776f5cce17735416001b1429cc41a82094ee84b46f2c8e13938d522c1c"}}

{"body": {"notes": "Wood is a song I wrote and self produced.  Released in December of 2019 after months away from home on tour.  Drained but with good intentions.  Sad but hopeful.  I remember being obsessed with wood during the time of making this song, which is probably how it got this title.  Wood as in the material.  I started to buy a bunch of hand-crafted wooden furniture/designs for my studio and was super into the texture, the smell, the feel of it.  I wasn't sure why my heart was pulled to it.  One day I got a tarot card reading and the person literally said, "Putting yourself around wood would be really good for you right now, something grounding... try to maybe go to a forrest". I'm open minded of course but it was definitely odd to hear the synchronicities in the tarot-readers advice.  Maybe I smelled like wood. 

It's part of the V2 series which is more so, stream of consciousness styled stuff.  Almost with a demo-structure to it rather than songs that abide by some rule of arrangement.   

I'm happy this song is out in the world.  I had a deep seated feeling of fear before putting it out, because of how vulnerable it was.  But if I've learned anything that feeling is usually a good sign that you're telling the truth.", "title": "Wood V2", "artist": "Felly", "artwork": {"nft": null, "info": {"uri": "https://ipfs.io/ipfs/bafybeieos2ywqzhpeuep5u47wfwkroyyw5t727jzdwl4cqx4pz4udetema", "mimeType": "image/jpeg"}, "isNft": false}, "project": null, "version": "catalog-20210202", "duration": 244.872, "mimeType": "audio/x-wav", "visualizer": null, "trackNumber": null}, "origin": {"encoding": "rlp", "algorithm": "secp256k1", "publicKey": "0xc236541380fc0C2C05c2F2c6c52a21ED57c37952", "signature": "0x16b239648bbb96b4c8fcf33c34c7da504fa7a2e8b5c1330c76209267b6f0b9a7154cbe689f65e1af2ce6bbdf757091946ca2e250e3df3bc54ffb4b30bc8634cb1b"}}

